messages:
elaine: Hey folks — I'm opening a tiny cleanup PR to the hello quickstart. Focus: make the auth examples explicit and add a small server-proxy snippet so people don't accidentally paste keys in the browser. Will include Docker non-root and a HEALTHCHECK.

matt: solid. Can we also show the minimal ENV approach + header approach side-by-side? A single toggle makes it easier for readers.

elaine: yep — two columns in the snippet (env vs header) and a short note: never commit .env.

sophia: I'll add .dockerignore and suggest USER 1001 in Dockerfile. Also add a line about mounting .env for local dev: `docker run --env-file .env local-hello`.

juna: For the proxy example, recommend a tiny Express handler and mention CORS. Quick snippet idea:
```js
// proxy.js (very small)
const express = require('express');
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/api/generate', async (req, res) => {
  const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify(req.body)
  });
  const body = await r.json();
  res.json(body);
});
app.listen(3000);
```

elaine: nice and compact. Add a short security note: rotate keys, use KMS for production.

matt: Quick nit: include Content-Type in curl examples and show a streaming vs non-streaming example callout. People often forget to set `Accept: text/event-stream` when testing SSE.

sophia: Added a `.env.example` with REDWOOD_API_KEY=your_key_here and a README snippet about checking for trailing spaces. I also caught a broken relative link in the README that pointed to `/examples/old-hello` — fixed in the draft.

docs-bot: Docs PR checklist: examples under /examples, include runnable Dockerfile, run linkcheck, add label `quickstart-onboard`.

elaine: PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/823 — includes: proxy example, non-root Dockerfile, .env.example, updated curl/SDK v4 snippets, and a short v3 migration footnote.

preview-bot: Deploy preview created for PR 823: https://deploy-preview.redwood.ai/quickstart/hello-proxy. Linkcheck running.

matt: I'll do a brief review after standup. If it's quick I'll approve.

juna: I'll smoke-test on linux VM and report back. Looking for: proxy forwarding, docker env load, and healthcheck responding.

sophia: small find: in the SDK example we used `client.generate({input})` but the public API is `client.text.generate({input})` in v4 — I'll update before review.

elaine: thanks — push that fix. Also adding a 1-line troubleshooting section: common errors (invalid_key, 401, ECONNRESET).

preview-bot: Linkcheck: 1 warning (relative anchor mismatch), sample-run: ok.

matt: Reviewed. LGTM once the anchor warning is addressed. Two tiny wording suggestions in the auth paragraph.

elaine: fixed the anchor and wording. Re-pushed.

preview-bot: Updated preview: https://deploy-preview.redwood.ai/quickstart/hello-proxy — all checks green.

juna: Smoke test results: proxy forwards correctly, docker healthcheck passes, env mount works. No flakes on linux.

elaine: thanks everyone. I'll merge and backport the short v3 migration line. Will also follow up with a separate issue to add a brief lab exercise for onboarding. :tada:
